+# v33 — map-settling recovery and daily gem collection
+
+- Late movement after a map drag no longer immediately stops the fixed route.
+  Reuse the pre-click screenshot, recognise the settled map, recalculate the
+  same world target and reveal it again if needed. Stable checks add no fixed
+  wait or extra screenshot. Unrecognisable or continuously moving maps still
+  stop without marking an unchecked location complete.
+- Gem Sniper runs continuously until five sightings in the current game day
+  or Stop/F10. Both start buttons and the hotkey use this daily loop.
+- After each confirmed gem, save its photo and click its centre, wait 20
+  cancellable seconds, select Emerald Corner (241,107), confirm and close
+  the map, then click the gameplay centre to return the character.
+- Return after the fifth find too, then stop without starting a sixth pass,
+  including when the collection wait crosses the 16:00 game-day reset.
+  Earlier finds restart at the selected route's first point with fresh map
+  recognition. Total elapsed time, finds and completed-pass times are retained.
+- The worker uses the same persistent seen ledger as the header/history with
+  its own SQLite connections. Existing counts, screenshot updates and UI event
+  replays cannot bypass or double-increment the goal. Already 5/5 blocks input
+  before starting. The game day still resets at 16:00 Europe/Sofia.
+- F10 interrupts collection and return, releases mouse input and never
+  restarts the worker. An unconfirmed return camera sends no character click.
+- Teal sighting dots last exactly 1 hour and 15 seconds (3,615 seconds) from
+  the original sighting, with hour-aware countdown labels. Editing coordinates,
+  screenshot completion and restarting the app retain the original deadline.
+- Gem Spy remains observation-only, retains its separate encounter/hourly
+  histories, and does not increment or stop at the Sniper daily goal.
+- v32 native cursor guards, confirmed gem edge clicks, four map-control boxes
+  with no padding, removed portal restrictions, route editing/profiles and
+  all assets are retained in the newly built EXE and complete source folder.
+
+Validation covers delayed map frames using actual atlas terrain; quota,
+collection, restart, exact return and cancellation simulations; native Windows
+UI/storage/detector integration; real Win32 input against a test window; the
+frozen EXE; and complete archive extraction/hash verification. These checks do
+not constitute a live BlueStacks game run. No private recordings are packaged.
